{
  "_comment": [
    "Feed-shaped sources. Adding an outlet is a line here, not a new fetcher.",
    "",
    "`tier` is the one piece of editorial judgement in this file and `impact`",
    "leans on it more than on anything else:",
    "  1 = primary source publishing the thing itself - a central bank, a",
    "      statistical agency, a regulator. No commentary outranks the statement.",
    "  2 = a wire or a major outlet reporting it, or a central bank's own",
    "      research blog: reliable, fast, but a report of an event.",
    "  3 = analysis, newsletters and individual writers. Frequently the most",
    "      useful reading here and almost never the news itself.",
    "",
    "`hint` is a category from categorize.CATEGORIES, applied when neither the",
    "keyword pass nor the LLM has a better idea - a liquidity newsletter is",
    "about monetary policy even when a given post's headline does not say so.",
    "",
    "All 25 feeds verified reachable on 2026-09-19 with this project's own user",
    "agent. A dead one fails soft and is reported by `cli fetch`; it never",
    "breaks the run.",
    "",
    "Known gap: the BLS blocks automated clients entirely (HTTP 403), so CPI and",
    "payrolls arrive here through the wires rather than from the agency. The",
    "numbers themselves come from FRED, which is unaffected."
  ],
